[0168] As an example, suppose V.sub.k/V.sub.w=10, K.sub.1=1.2 and K.sub.d=0.1. In such a way, KPF=20 would be obtained.

[0169] Supposing the air density .rho. constant and equal to 1.225 kg/m.sup.3, the specific power generated by the Specific Wind Power would be:

SpecificWindPower = 1 2 .rho. V w 3 = 0.5 * 1.225 * 6 3 = 132.3 W / m 2 ##EQU00001##

[0170] The power that can be generated by means of the kite, KitePower, is expressed by the following formula:

KitePower=KPF*SpecificWindPower*A

[0171] If, for example, a kite were used with a surface of 18 m.sup.2 pushed at the speed of 60 m/s by a wind blowing at 6 m/s, the power that it would be possible to generate at rope level would be 47628 W. Such power would correspond therefore to the maximum power that the kite is able to generate.

[0172] The value assumed by KPF anyway depends on the kite efficiency. It is possible to make KPF assume values greater than 20. If for example KPF assumed a value equal to 40, the maximum power that can be obtained by a kite whose area is 18 m.sup.2 would be 95256 W.

